  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1235 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThursday night through Monday:\n\nLow pressure begins an eastward retreat Thursday, with any\nlingering rain chances (20-40%) tapering down Thursday night into\nFriday. A northerly breeze on Friday will return temperatures to \nseasonal norms (highs around 50, lows in the 30s), where they'll\nhold through Saturday before beginning a slight warming trend\ninto early next week. Predominantly dry weather is looking \nlikely on Saturday, but a handful of ensemble members suggest a \npossible clipper system Saturday night through Sunday with \nchances for rain. Holding precip chances around 20% late this \nweekend until models converge on the presence and track of said \nsystem.\n\nSheppard",
